rgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-05T19:21:10Z","updated_at":"2025-08-05T19:21:10Z","body":"> Hm, now that I think about it, @scgm0 , may I ask if you can compile the engine with `builtin_sdl=no` flag and test the issue (without applying this PR)? (You may need to install SDL with your OS package manager)\r\n\r\nUsing `builtin_sdl=no` allows it to run properly.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3156314018/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3156325986","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109283#issuecomment-3156325986","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109283","id":3156325986,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc68IbZi","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-05T19:26:16Z","updated_at":"2025-08-05T19:26:31Z","body":"Thank you, and good, then that sounds like an issue that should be possible to get fixed, I will see what I can do later!","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3156325986/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3168327479","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109283#issuecomment-3168327479","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109283","id":3168327479,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc682Nc3","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-08T15:34:30Z","updated_at":"2025-08-08T15:34:30Z","body":"@scgm0 @DanielSnd Hello, I've got a new approach at solving this problem and I've already pushed it here. I think the problem has something to do with this line: `extern char **environ;` (because that's essentially what the preprocessor outputs from the lines mentioned in the original message if all 3 of the defines are defined), and I checked what SDL uses to get environment variables in order to ignore unnecessary gamepads (so Steam Input can function properly), the search led me to `SDL_getenv` (not `SDL_getenv_unsafe` which I thought initially), so I decided to use `getenv` inside `SDL_getenv` directly instead of `SDL_GetEnvironmentVariable` (which relies on `environ` variable). Let's hope this works.\r\n\r\nMay I ask if you can test the issues with this new approach, if you're not busy of course?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3168327479/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3169067892","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109283#issuecomment-3169067892","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109283","id":3169067892,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc685CN0","user":{"login":"scgm0","id":52148221,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMTQ4MjIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52148221?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0","html_url":"https://github.com/scgm0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-08T19:20:43Z","updated_at":"2025-08-08T19:20:43Z","body":"> @scgm0 @DanielSnd Hello, I've got a new approach at solving this problem and I've already pushed it here. I think the problem has something to do with this line: `extern char **environ;` (because that's essentially what the preprocessor outputs from the lines mentioned in the original message if all 3 of the defines are defined), and I checked what SDL uses to get environment variables in order to ignore unnecessary gamepads (so Steam Input can function properly), the search led me to `SDL_getenv` (not `SDL_getenv_unsafe` which I thought initially), so I decided to use `getenv` inside `SDL_getenv` directly instead of `SDL_GetEnvironmentVariable` (which relies on `environ` variable). Let's hope this works.\r\n> \r\n> May I ask if you can test the issues with this new approach, if you're not busy of course?\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1282\" height=\"806\" alt=\"图片\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f68658b4-5594-4a69-a50e-9ccc6abca73e\" />\r\nTested the GitHub auto-build template, no issues found.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3169067892/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3169177388","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109283#issuecomment-3169177388","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109283","id":3169177388,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc685c8s","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.co